\f1\fs22 \'93What\'92s the meaning of this congregation?\'94 he demanded, tugging at his white jumpsuit with its embroidered cross-guitar emblem.\
A nervous Elvi server averted his eyes.\
Humble\'92s pompadour quivered with suspicion. \'93Whats going on the stasis store?\'94\
Before anyone could answer, a sound emerged from the cooler\'97a rhythmic thumping accompanied by muffled exclamations that were decidedly not prayers, at least not of any denomination Humble recognised.\
He yanked open the heavy steel door and saw a tableau that would have given Hieronymus Bosch pause: a dozen Elvi engaged in activities that were biblical without being holy. He knew the sin of lust when he saw it and heard it. He knew the when the sanctity of cleaving and becoming one flesh was being corrupted by base desires, he knew when organs were placed in orifices that would never lead to conception, and he knew when there were too many participants involved to be holy in God\'92s eyes. Writhing between hanging sides of pork was clearly off-script, as was knocking containers of spices and marinades from shelves, as was transforming a prep table into an altar of an entirely different religion.\
\'93Blasphemy!\'94 Humble roared, his voice cracking like lightning across the frigid air.\
The copulating Elvi froze, but their sequinned jumpsuits still sparkled. Leather pants remained down around their knees.\
\'93Pastor Rex!\'94 gasped an Elvine called Memphis Marguerita. \'93We were just spreading\'97\'94\
\'93I can see what you are spreading, girl.\'94 Humble\'92s eyes were ablaze and his brows were smouldering, as he read teh slogan on her dishevelled tee shirt: 
\f2\i Give Them the Hump
\f1\i0 .\
\'93She is sharing the Great Teacher\'92s gift with us\'97so we may be free of the pestilence.\'94\
\'93The pestilence is God\'92s curse on the iniquitous, and a blessing for the righteous, for they shall be spared,\'94 Humble preached. \'93Hear me, servants of the true faith! Let no Gospel Elvi shall believe the lies of false prophets! We shall remain pure and let faith shield us from earthly plagues!\'94\
For the most part, Gospel Elvi stood firm in their rejection of bacchanalian fornication, and rather took to fervently praying and singing hymns over their sick.\
Some of the pious wavered, those who noticed Evolution Elvi recovering from illness and then the dwindling numbers in their social circles of Evolution Elvi falling sick at all. In fact, they appeared healthier than than they\'92d ever been before.\
A few days later, Pastor Rex Humble succumbed, his fever-wracked body collapsed over his makeshift pulpit. As consciousness faded, he gazed up at the neon-lit ceiling of his once-thriving Gospel House, now empty save for a few equally doomed acolytes. In his last moments, he couldn't help but wonder if perhaps Darwin had been onto something after all.
